{
  "_README": [
    "TEMPLATE 6 — /about/team  (THREE team members)",
    "",
    "=========================================================================",
    "READ THIS FIRST: a three-person team page is NOT a ProfilePage.",
    "=========================================================================",
    "Google's ProfilePage requirement is explicit: 'The primary focus of the page must be a",
    "single person or organization.' A page listing three people has three primary subjects, so",
    "it fails that test. ProfilePage takes one mainEntity, not a list.",
    "",
    "I recommended ProfilePage for this page in an earlier note. That was wrong and this",
    "template supersedes it.",
    "",
    "CORRECT STRUCTURE FOR A TEAM PAGE:",
    "    CollectionPage  +  ItemList  +  three Person nodes, each with a stable @id",
    "",
    "WHEN ProfilePage IS CORRECT:",
    "    One page per person — /about/team/will-gibson — with mainEntity being that one Person.",
    "    Google's own examples of valid profile pages include 'an employee page on a company",
    "    website', so individual pages qualify; the roster page does not.",
    "",
    "SHOULD YOU BUILD INDIVIDUAL PAGES? Not yet. Three thin bio pages are worse than one good",
    "team page. Build them only when a person has enough substance to justify a URL: a real",
    "biography, verifiable credentials, and ideally authored content on the site. Will Gibson is",
    "the likely first candidate if he is authoring the resources pages. Until then, the stable",
    "@ids below do the same job — they give each person a permanent identifier that Article",
    "author references can point at.",
    "",
    "RICH RESULT ELIGIBILITY: Breadcrumbs only. Person and ProfilePage produce no rich result.",
    "The value is E-E-A-T and entity understanding, which is exactly what you want if these",
    "people are going to be named as authors.",
    "",
    "Strip all _README and _comment keys before shipping."
  ],

  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [

    {
      "_comment": "SHARED BUSINESS NODE — ship the COMPLETE version from _business-node.jsonld.",
